From a05ff2c8a6f9ba2713b69739b19cf806faf3e4c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 08:38:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pgxp: model the SXYP FIFO push in the GTE register shadows -
 the GT2 track seams

ROOT CAUSE. Guest writes to SXYP (GTE data reg 15) are a FIFO push on hardware:
SXY0<-SXY1, SXY1<-SXY2, SXY2<-new. gte_write_data shifted the REAL registers
but the PGXP shadows for 12..14 were left describing the pre-push words. The
old comment called this acceptable ('validation drops them on next use').
It is not: the next SWC2 of SXY0/1/2 runs pv_validate, sees value != actual,
strips the X/Y flags and copies a FLAGLESS shadow into the display list. The
GPU then draws that corner at its rounded integer position while the adjacent
face - whose copy came straight from RTPS - keeps its fraction. Two faces of
one mesh disagree about a shared corner by up to a pixel. At 16x that is a
16-pixel line of whatever lies behind the track.

GT2's race overlay does this constantly: its strip builder loads three cached
projections with lwc2 into SXY0..2, NCLIPs, stores them with swc2, then
pushes a fourth through SXYP (mtc2 gte15 at 0x80024E10) to NCLIP the quad's
other triangle - and the same 'reinject a cached projection' idiom is all over
the track code (0x80025444/48, 0x80025538/3C, 0x80025698/A0/B0, ...).

Measured on Tahiti at the grid, same savestate:
  mixed triangles (1-2 of 3 corners precise) per 3s :  ~1600 -> 0
  shared-EDGE corners on track faces that disagree  :   702 -> 0
  swc2 sites whose SXY shadow != stored word        :  100% -> 0% at every site
  teal seam pixels in the hires frame               :  3513 -> ~0

Design, with the ordering every caller already has (gte_write_data, then the
PGXP cop2 hook):
  - gte_write_data case 15 notifies pgxp_gte_reg_written(15) ONLY, which
    shifts the shadow FIFO and leaves a value-only shadow in 14/15.
  - The LWC2/MTC2 hook for rt/rd==15 does NOT shift again; it replaces 14/15
    with the source's real precision. rt/rd==14 mirrors into 15 likewise.
  - gte_write_data case 14 no longer notifies 15: SXYP mirrors SXY2, it is not
    a push. Treating it as one shifted SXY0/SXY1 on every lwc2 of SXY2 and
    broke every load-three/NCLIP/store sequence (measured: reg12/13 100% bad,
    reg14 fine - the signature that located it).

Diagnostics that found it, kept: per-slot last-writer provenance (wr_instr/
wr_pc), the mixed-primitive census (pgxp_mixed), the resolved-corner ring
(pgxp_tris) with the offline seam analyser, and per-site swc2 shadow health
(pgxp_swc2).
---
